From 1072d43de5adb4e2b8b8f6b62a85e8bbff5585b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:57:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] feat(mcp): batch read-only exec commands in one request

exec rejected any request holding more than one command (A3), so an
agent's discovery (search, info, schema, read-only calls) cost one
request each.

Up to 10 read-only commands can now share a request, one per line: help,
tools, search, info, schema, and call on a tool annotated readOnlyHint:
true. They run in order and each result comes back under its own label;
a failing command returns its error in its place. A batch holding a call
to any other tool, or a learn, is refused whole before anything runs, so
writes stay one per request and confirmable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
